# REGENT OF TRENGGALEK,

Considering:  
a. that the Unitary State of the Republic of Indonesia guarantees the welfare of each of its citizens, including protection of women's rights and children's rights which are human rights;  
b. that in order to improve the position, role, and quality of women is an effort to realize gender equality and justice in family, community, national, and state life;  
c. that every child is a bud, potential, and successor generation of the nation's struggle, and is expected to be able to bear that responsibility in the future, therefore they need to be given the widest possible opportunity to grow and develop optimally, both physically, mentally and socially, and have noble character, so that protection efforts need to be made and to realize child welfare by providing guarantees for the fulfillment of their rights and the existence of treatment without discrimination;  
d. that violence against women and children is a crime against humanity which constitutes a violation of human rights;  

2 -
e. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, letter c, and letter d, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Implementation of Protection of Women and Children;  

In View of:  
