# CHAPTER IV

## PROTECTION OF CHILDREN

## Part One

Rights and Obligations of Children

#### Article 10

Every child has the right:
a. to survival, growth, development and participation in a reasonable manner in accordance with human dignity and to receive protection from violence and discrimination;  
b. to a name as personal identity and citizenship status;  
c. to worship according to his/her religion, to think, and to express in accordance with the level of intelligence and age, under parental guidance;  
d. to know his/her parents, to be raised, and cared for by his/her own parents;  
e. to obtain health services and social security in accordance with physical, mental, spiritual, and social needs; f. to obtain education and teaching in the context of developing his/her personality and level of intelligence in accordance with interests and talents;  
g. to express and be heard his/her opinion, to receive, seek, and provide information in accordance with the level of intelligence and age for self-development in accordance with moral values and propriety;  
h. to rest and utilize leisure time, to associate with peers, to play, to recreate, and to create in accordance with interests, talents, and level of intelligence for self-development;  
i. to receive protection from discriminatory treatment, exploitation, whether economic or sexual, neglect, violence, abuse, injustice, other mistreatment, while in the care of parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for care;  

17 -
j. to be cared for by his/her own parents, unless there are reasons and/or valid legal rules showing that the separation is in the best interests of the child and is a last resort; andk. to obtain protection from abuse in political activities, involvement in armed conflicts, involvement in social unrest, involvement in events containing elements of violence and involvement in warfare.

#### Article 11

1. Every child has the right to obtain protection from being the target of persecution, torture, or imposition of inhuman punishment.  
2. Every child has the right to obtain freedom in accordance with the law.  
3. Arrest, detention, or criminal imprisonment of a child shall only be carried out if in accordance with applicable law and can only be carried out as a last resort.
